# DataSource Pattern

DataSources define schema, permissions, and lifecycle hooks for database tables. They live under `src/lib/common/ds/definitions/` and register via `src/lib/common/ds/registry.ts`.

## Basic Shape

```typescript
import type { DataSource } from "@/lib/common/ds/types";
import { DefaultAttribute, DefaultDataSource } from "@/lib/common/ds/defaults";
import type { Entity } from "@/lib/common/ds/types/module/Entity";

export const EntityDataSource: DataSource<Entity> = {
  ...DefaultDataSource,
  id: "Entity",
  tableName: "entity",
  description: "One row per entity. Written by users on the Entities page.",
  attributes: [
    {
      ...DefaultAttribute,
      code: "id",
      name: "ID",
      type: "Text",
      column: "id",
      primary: true,
      maxLength: 40,
      optional: false,
      description: "Primary key, UUIDv7 generated on insert.",
    },
    {
      ...DefaultAttribute,
      code: "name",
      name: "Name",
      type: "Text",
      column: "name",
      maxLength: 120,
      optional: false,
      description: "Short name shown in lists.",
    },
    {
      ...DefaultAttribute,
      code: "createdAt",
      name: "Created At",
      type: "Date",
      column: "created_at",
      optional: false,
      description: "Timestamp when record was created (auto-populated).",
    },
    {
      ...DefaultAttribute,
      code: "createdBy",
      name: "Created By",
      type: "Text",
      column: "created_by",
      maxLength: 128,
      optional: false,
      description: "User who created the record (auto-populated).",
    },
  ],
  access: {
    query: "AUTHENTICATED",
    insert: "AUTHENTICATED",
    update: "AUTHENTICATED",
    delete: "AUTHENTICATED",
  },
};
```

## Descriptions (Required)

Every DataSource and every attribute must have a `description`:
- **DataSource**: what one row represents, who writes it, how it is scoped
- **Attribute**: what the value means, format/unit, allowed values, relationships

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
{ code: 'amount', name: 'Amount', column: 'amount' }

// ✅ Good
{ 
  code: 'amount', 
  name: 'Amount', 
  column: 'amount',
  description: 'Amount in USD; decimals allowed.'
}
```

## Attribute Types

| Type | Use | Properties |
|------|-----|-----------|
| `Text` | String values | `maxLength` |
| `Number` | Numeric values | `allowDecimals` |
| `Date` | Date/datetime | - |
| `Boolean` | True/false | - |

## Lifecycle Hooks

Hooks run in transaction boundaries and validate, transform, or audit data:

### Query Hooks

```typescript
export const EntityDataSource: DataSource<Entity> = {
  // Modify query before execution (scope rows by user)
  preQuery: async ({ query, session, client }) => {
    if (!session.user.isAdmin) {
      query.filters = [...(query.filters || []), { userId: { is: session.user.id } }];
    }
    return query;
  },

  // Post-process query results
  postQuery: async ({ query, rows, session, client }) => {
    return rows.map(row => ({
      ...row,
      displayName: `${row.firstName} ${row.lastName}`,
    }));
  },
};
```

### Insert/Update/Delete Hooks

```typescript
import { UserError } from "@wayvo-ai/core/common";

export const EntityDataSource: DataSource<Entity> = {
  // Validate before insert
  beforeInsert: async ({ rows, session, client }) => {
    for (const row of rows) {
      if (!row.name?.trim()) {
        throw new UserError('Name is required');
      }
      if (!row.status) {
        row.status = 'draft';  // Set defaults
      }
    }
    return { rows };
  },

  // Post-insert side effects (notifications, cascade)
  afterInsert: async ({ rows, session, client }) => {
    // Runs in same transaction
    return rows;
  },

  // Validate before update
  beforeUpdate: async ({ rows, session, client }) => {
    for (const row of rows) {
      if (row.status === 'published' && !row.publishedAt) {
        row.publishedAt = new Date().toISOString();
      }
    }
    return { rows };
  },

  // Post-update side effects
  afterUpdate: async ({ rows, session, client }) => {
    return rows;
  },

  // Validate before delete; `previousRows` are from DB
  beforeDelete: async ({ rows, previousRows, session, client }) => {
    for (const row of previousRows ?? []) {
      if (row.isProtected) {
        throw new UserError('Cannot delete protected records');
      }
    }
    return rows;
  },

  // Post-delete cleanup (cascade delete)
  afterDelete: async ({ rows, session, client }) => {
    return rows;
  },
};
```

### Hook Reference

| Hook | When | Receives | Returns |
|------|------|----------|---------|
| `preQuery` | Before query execution | `query, session, client` | Modified `Query<T>` |
| `postQuery` | After query results | `query, rows, session, client` | Modified `DBRow<T>[]` |
| `beforeInsert` | Before insert | `rows, session, client` | `{ rows, skipDML? }` |
| `afterInsert` | After insert | `rows, session, client` | `DBRow<T>[]` |
| `beforeUpdate` | Before update | `rows, session, client` | `{ rows, skipDML? }` |
| `afterUpdate` | After update | `rows, session, client` | `DBRow<T>[]` |
| `beforeDelete` | Before delete | `rows, previousRows, session, client` | `DBRow<T>[]` |
| `afterDelete` | After delete | `rows, session, client` | `DBRow<T>[]` |

**Important:** 
- Throw `UserError` for user-facing validation errors; it shows to the user and rolls back the transaction
- All other errors log to server and show generic message to user
- Hooks run within the same database transaction as the main operation

## Cascade Delete Pattern

Use `afterDelete` to cleanup related records:

```typescript
afterDelete: async ({ rows, client }) => {
  if (rows.length === 0) return rows;
  
  for (const row of rows) {
    const projectId = row.projectId;
    if (projectId) {
      await client.query(`DELETE FROM project_tasks WHERE project_id = $1`, [projectId]);
      await client.query(`DELETE FROM project_roles WHERE project_id = $1`, [projectId]);
    }
  }
  
  return rows;
},
```

